course: dictionary
lesson: 12084
title: Closure: an ending, a feeling, a lid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word closure comes from close, which means to shut or to finish. A closure is the act of closing something. «The school closure for snow meant no lessons on Monday.» Here closure means a school was shut for a time.
explain: Closure can also be a feeling. «After the match, Sam finally got closure about losing.» When something sad or upsetting has ended and you can move on, you have closure. The context tells you this is about feelings, not doors.
explain: Closure can be a thing too, like a lid or zip that closes something. This meaning is formal, so you will mostly meet it in writing. «The jar had a tight metal closure, so nothing spilled.» A jar needs a lid to stop things spilling, so closure means the thing that closes it.
fact: Closure means the closing of a place or business, for a time or for ever.
fact: «The closure of the road» means the road has been shut.
fact: Closure can mean a feeling that something sad or upsetting has ended, so you can move on.
fact: Closure can also mean something that closes a thing, like a lid or zip (formal).
fact: Closure is a noun. You can count closures, but when you talk about a feeling it is uncountable: you get closure, not a closure.
exercise: «The school closure for snow meant no lessons on Monday.» What does closure mean here? | *The closing of a school for a time | A new school uniform | A big school hall | A school trip to the zoo
exercise: «After the match, Sam finally got closure about losing.» What does closure mean here? | A lost ball | *A feeling that something sad has ended, so you can move on | A new match to play | A loud cheer from the crowd
exercise: «The jar had a tight metal closure, so nothing spilled.» What is the closure? | A big wooden spoon | *The lid or zip that closes it | The table the jar stood on | The label on the jar
test: Nadia says closure is just a fancy word for a door. Which reply is best? | Yes, it always means a door | It is a type of bird | *No, it can mean a shut place, a feeling that something has ended, or a lid | It means a lot of noise
test: «Factory closures left many people without jobs.» What does closures mean? | Big parties for the workers | Shiny new machines | Long summer holidays by the sea | *Places that have shut, for a time or for ever
exam: «She wanted closure after the argument, so she talked to her friend.» What does closure mean here? | A new shop opening nearby | A loud noise from the street | *A feeling that the upsetting argument has ended | A tight zip on her bag
